Rust looks like a hopeful early-access survival game, 7/10 for now -someweirdonamedsilver
More objective part: graphics depend on your rig, they can range from "which pixel is my character?"
To good enough;
The survival some time ago adopted an RPG element to crafting, in which you unlock the ability to craft stuff by using level points gained by doing survival stuff, I think it's garbage,
Because it's unfair with people new to the server, but it's rust so no one cares about what's unfair,
AI is comprety garbage;
Gameplay it's fine-ish, sometimes some annoying glitches happen;
KOS, kill on sight, believe me I've died dozens of times for making goodhearted choices.
Vast base building system;
More subjective part, and hints:
If you don't play it with friends at first you'll maybe want to give up on it
Since this game can get immensely frustrating
But the best way to deal with fails is respawning and building it all up again
It is a good survival game overall, the developers STILL need to adress the bugged animals
If you couldn't kill a horse within 5 seconds just let it go, because they just go through rocks and climb cliffs
Like there weren't any cliffs in the first place,
And avoid wolves and bears if you don't have ranged weapons at all costs,
Bears almost insta kill and wolves, if they get you by surprise, will kill you easily,
But do not, DO NOT! Ever trust anyone, I know it's cliche, but it's just a fact,
Don't even trust people who seem to be beginners (nakeds) they will stab first chance they get,
Be Professional, and always have a plan to kill players around you;
Oh and yea, I hope you don't mind racial slurs because those guys love it;
The best way to deal with players is, if they have spotted you, kill them quickly and if you couldn't, don't chase them
Unless you KNOW for sure it's worth it,
But expect that person to be back with friends;
If not spotted, just avoid or wait for the perfect moment;
Build base clever base designs, making it harder for raiders to get to the loot,
Be sure to have two different exits, and optionally, an advanced post hidden nearby with weapons on it, in case you die;
That load of crap was my third review, please feel free to criticize and do whatever else you want.

Pro:
1. Daily dev updates;
2. Lots of server; official and modded.
Cons:
1. Still in alpha;
2. Players can be bloodthirsty, even to noobs;
3. Hackers roam the land, griefing others.
Recommendation: play with a friend, for security and fun.

